        "id": 181404,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2016-08-26T20:57:05.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I ordered some of the UltraPro, 9 card pages, transparent on both sides and put all the foil cards (already sleeved) into the pages. Put the pages in a folder. Then just barely managed to stop myself from taking the folder to work and trying to convince my co-workers to look at all the pretty, pretty cards.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>While putting the cards in the pages, I began thinking about the possibility of _ALSO_ putting a set of all of the original artwork into the pages as well. I have all of the original variants, so when the complete variant set ships, I could put all the original variants in the pages and use the complete set of variants for actual play.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>But what would I do for the original artwork on the primary character cards for each hero? I am not buying a complete set of the core and expansion games just to get a second set of those primary character cards.</p>",
