        "created_at": "2016-08-26T21:00:02.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"arenson9\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/48/1900_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> arenson9:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I ordered some of the UltraPro, 9 card pages, transparent on both sides and put all the foil cards (already sleeved) into the pages. Put the pages in a folder. Then just barely managed to stop myself from taking the folder to work and trying to convince my co-workers to look at all the pretty, pretty cards.&nbsp;While putting the cards in the pages, I began thinking about the possibility of <em>ALSO</em> putting a set of all of the original artwork into the pages as well. I have all of the original variants, so when the complete variant set ships, I could put all the original variants in the pages and use the complete set of variants for actual play.&nbsp;But what would I do for the original artwork on the primary character cards for each hero? I am not buying a complete set of the core and expansion games just to get a second set of those primary character cards.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Order them as replacement cards?</p>",
